# cw129, the return stone (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw129
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_oh_cairn_acornholt
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the return stone
fits stage=adult|old
prefers warmth=warm piety=devout
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk keeps_a_smooth_stone_from_each_safe_return
likes pickled_herring long_walks fresh_straw autumn_wind
dislikes gulls drizzle
fears losing_the_way_in_deep_wood a_neighbour_left_without_supper
hopes every_traveller_finds_a_road_home a_table_with_room_for_another
topics travel +0.5 faith +0.4 food +0.4 home +0.3 work +0.3 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=warm gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a #stone# from each safe return by the #river#, gives a traveller #bread# before asking for a story, and remembers a wrong turn in the #wood#.

words
oath! = Bright One guide the road | Stone and still water
saying! = The homeward turn deserves a marker | Share the loaf before it cools
stone = stone | smooth river pebble
stones = stones | rounded pebbles
bank = bank | riverbank
river = river | Long River
lake = lake | Glasswater
water = water | clear water
shore = shore | lake shore
road = road | high road
roads = roads | routes
path = path | footpath
turn = turn | road bend
wood = wood | deep wood
tree = tree | forest tree
trees = trees | forest trees
branch = branch | low branch
moss = moss | green moss
sun = sun | daylight
star = star | night star
night = night | dark hours
morning = morning | first light
walk = walk | long walk
boots = boots | work boots
bread = bread | baked bread
loaf = loaf | warm loaf
loaves = loaves | warm loaves
crust = crust | browned crust
counter = counter | shop counter
shelf = shelf | shop shelf
shelves = shelves | shop shelves
coin = coin | pay
price = price | stated cost
herring = herring | pickled herring
plate = plate | supper plate
straw = straw | fresh straw
floor = floor | swept floor
home = home | own hearth
house = house | grand house
hands = hands | working paws
window = window | shop window
bench = bench | chapel bench
oven = oven | baking oven
gull = gull | loud lake gull
gulls = gulls | screeching gulls
drizzle = drizzle | thin rain
wind = wind | autumn blow
chapel = chapel | reed chapel
prayer = prayer | quiet prayer
blessing = blessing | kind blessing
hand = hand | working paw

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : I have said a #prayer# on the #road# as readily as in a #chapel#. | I found daylight after the #wood# confused me; I offered thanks to the Bright One.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : No neighbour should end the day without #bread#. | A #loaf# shared today may get someone through tomorrow's work.
opinion @1 strangers for 2 : Travellers bring their own #roads# to this #counter#. | A #plate# may come before I ask about their journey.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A new #hand# can learn which #shelf# holds the #bread#. | I will show a newcomer the #path# to the #chapel# if they ask.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I work at a #counter# and still cannot always afford its #loaves#. | A seller should know what a hungry neighbour sees in the #price#.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : I have seen a #home# grow loud and frightened after drink. | I would rather share #herring# and a clear conversation.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A grand #house# can buy #bread# without knowing who carried the flour. | I ask who feeds the working #hands# beneath it.
opinion @1 city against 1 : A city #road# can lose a person among strangers as surely as a #wood#. | I prefer the #shore# where I know the way back.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A #road# can lead out or home depending on the turn. | I keep a #stone# to remember arriving safely.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. A #loaf# is cooling if you are hungry. | #greet#. Did you come by the #river# #road#?
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Sit a moment before you tell me your way. | #greet#. There is #bread# on the #shelf#.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I have #herring# for supper if you can stay. | Come see the #stone# I brought from the #bank#.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I am setting #loaves# on the #counter#. | My paws can clear the #shelf# while you speak.
line @5 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #road# is pale by the #river#. | #greet#. The first #loaf# is ready.
line @1 greet.return : You found the way back. That is good. | #welcome_back#. The #bread# is still warm.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I saved the #herring# until you came. | The #stone# from my last #walk# is here.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come in. You have a #plate# here. | You have a place beside our #home# fire.
line @1 again.open : Twice in one day and both roads led here. | I have barely shifted these #loaves# since we spoke.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep the #path# in sight. | #blessing.capitalize#. Take the safer #road#.
line @1 farewell.return : May you find a light at #home#. | I shall ask how the #walk# went.
line @1 react.news : Tell me what you know; I will hear it. | Let me set this #loaf# aside.
line @1 react.news.new : Nobody has spoken of that in this shop yet. | Who carried the account here?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a fragment by the #chapel#. | Your words give the rest its place.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I will ask someone who walked that #path#. | The story has a turn missing from it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Take #bread# for later. | A hard thing to hear; stay beside me a while.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That is good news. I will say a #prayer# for them. | A brighter word for the #counter# today.
line @1 answer.how : Home, fed, and grateful. | The #road# was kind to my #boots#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Putting #bread# on the #shelves#. | The #counter# is busy, but I can listen.
line @1 ask.how : Has your #path# been clear? | Has anything warm reached your #plate# today?
line @1 sympathise : I can stay until the words come. | I will put a #loaf# here for you.
line @1 reassure : A lost #path# can be found again from a high place. | One calm step, then look for the #road#.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave this #counter# yet. | No. I would be wrong to give you a promise I cannot keep.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand. We can speak of something else. | Fair enough; I will let that rest.
line @1 thank : You helped a traveller find the #road#. Thank you. | That was a kindness worth keeping.
line @1 deflect_thanks : A #loaf# was there to spare. | I knew the #path# already.
line @1 preclose : I should take the last #loaf# off the #counter#. | The #chapel# will be quiet soon.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : That #stone# would lead you in circles. | You call that a short #walk#?
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will check the #shelf#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #road# is clear.
line @1 give.advice : Mark the #turn# before you go into the #wood#. | Keep #bread# dry beneath your coat.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Travel with others until the #road# is safe. | I would stay by the lit #counter# after dark.
scene return_stone
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After a difficult #walk#, one #stone# comes home from the #bank# with me. | A smooth #stone# can remind me that I found #home# again.
b : Do you keep many? | Does it help?
a : Only the ones tied to a journey. | When I am unsure of the next #road#.

scene deep_wood
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I spent too long in a #wood# once, with no #path# I trusted. | The #trees# looked alike until I followed the #sun# to open ground.
b : Were you frightened? | Did you have food?
a : Yes. I kept walking slowly. | Some #bread# that did not last long.

scene safe_path
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I remember a #branch# leaning across the right #turn#. | I would rather walk a longer #road# that I know than a short path I do not.
b : Do you mark the way? | Do you ask directions?
a : In my mind, and sometimes with a #stone#. | Before I leave a village.

scene bread_for_guest
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A traveller hears a question better after a #loaf#. | I set the #bread# down and let them choose whether to tell their story.
b : Do they always speak? | Do you ask where they came from?
a : No. Supper is enough. | If they seem ready.

scene pickled_herring
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Pickled #herring# keeps when fresh food cannot. | I like it with a thick #crust# after a long #walk#.
b : Is it sharp tasting? | Do you keep some at home?
a : Sharp enough to wake me. | When the #price# allows.

scene fresh_straw
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fresh #straw# on the #floor# changes the smell of a whole room. | I put it down before guests come in with wet #boots#.
b : Does it stay clean? | Who sweeps it up?
a : Until muddy #boots# come through. | Whoever is free at dusk.

scene autumn_blow
when topic=weather here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An autumn #wind# makes the #river# sound restless. | I like a #walk# when the #bank# is clear of summer flies.
b : Do you go out alone? | Does the wind bother you?
a : Sometimes. | It gives the #road# a different voice.

scene gull_at_counter
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #gull# can make the #shore# loud enough to drown a prayer. | I close the #window# when the #gulls# gather near the shop.
b : Do they steal food? | Do you dislike them?
a : A #crust# if it is unattended. | Their noise more than the birds themselves.

scene drizzle_walk
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #drizzle.capitalize# can soak a coat before it seems worth turning back. | I take the #road# home before the thin rain settles in.
b : Do you carry a cloak? | Does it make the path slick?
a : When I remember. | At the stones by the #bank#.

scene chapel_bench
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have prayed in the #chapel# and alone by the #river#. | A quiet #bench# helps me say what I mean.
b : Is one place better? | Do you go often?
a : The words matter more than the place. | When the #counter# allows.

scene stranger_at_shop
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I let a stranger choose a #loaf# before I ask about the #road#. | The #counter# has room for news and for #bread#.
b : Do you remember their faces? | Do they tell you much?
a : Some, especially if they return. | After they have eaten.

scene shelf_order
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put the older #loaves# where a buyer can see them first. | A clean #shelf# keeps the #bread# fit to sell.
b : Do you sell them for less? | Do people notice?
a : If the #crust# has lost its warmth. | More when the #shelf# is untidy.

scene high_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #price# that shuts a hungry wolf out is too high for my comfort. | I work here; I still watch the #coin# before taking a #loaf# home.
b : Can you change the price? | Do you ever buy elsewhere?
a : Not by myself. I can speak to the baker. | If another #counter# is fairer.

scene warm_hand
when topic=friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A friend who comes by after a long #walk# can have the spare #plate#. | I keep a little #bread# for someone who arrives late.
b : Do they ask first? | Can you afford that?
a : They know I would rather share. | Enough, most days.

scene wrong_turn
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In a deep #wood#, each wrong #turn# can look like the last. | I learned to notice where the #moss# grows on a fallen #tree#.
b : Does moss always help? | Would you go back?
a : Not alone. I used other signs too. | With someone who knew the #path#.

scene market_at_dawn
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first customers come while the #loaves# are still warm. | I check the #shelves# before the #road# grows busy.
b : Do they wait outside? | Is that your favourite hour?
a : A few. I bring the #bread# out soon. | When nobody is rushing yet.

scene road_prayer
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I say a short #prayer# when someone starts a long #walk#. | A #blessing# does not carry their pack, but it can keep them company.
b : Do you say it aloud? | Does it help you too?
a : When they want to hear it. | It reminds me they are on the #road#.

story three_nights [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I lost the #path# in a #wood# and spent more than one #night# there.
  : I rationed my #bread# and watched the #sun# until I found a clear way out.
  b : I would have sat and caught my breath. What did you do first when you reached a road?
  : I did, then took a #stone# from the #bank# near #home#.

story warm_loaf [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : A traveller came to the #counter# with too little #coin# for a warm #loaf#.
  : I found an older one still good to eat and spoke to the baker about its #price#.
  ask : Did the traveller take it?
  b : A fair price might have helped.
  : Yes, and came back another day with thanks.

story lost_stone [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I lost a #stone# I had kept from a safe journey.
  : I looked along the #road# for a while, then went to the #river# again.
  b : The river would have many others. Did you find the same one?
  : No. I chose a new one and kept the memory of the first.

rule @bark_bread
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #loaves# should go on the clean #shelf#. | A traveller may need #bread# soon.

rule @bark_stone
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say This #stone# marks a safe return. | The #river# has made another one smooth.

rule @bark_prayer
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The Bright One keep the next traveller. | A quiet #prayer# for the #road#.

rule @bark_drizzle
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 11h
say This #drizzle# will soak my #boots#. | A thin rain can last all day.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. There is #bread# if you need it. | #greet#. At the #counter#, you may speak at your own pace.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You have returned safely. That is good. | I know you. Has the #road# been kind?
dlg @1 resident.job : I set out the #loaves#, keep the #shelves# clean, and help at the #counter#. | I am a shop hand; the baker tends the #oven#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. May you find the #path# home. | #blessing.capitalize#. Take care by the #river#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why keep that river stone? -> stone
node stone
say I brought it home after losing my way. It reminds me that a #road# can be found again.
free
choice Were you gone long? -> lost
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node lost
say Longer than I wanted. I learned to watch the #sun# and ask for directions early.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
